Package: OccurrenceCleaner
Title: Fast Quality Flags for Species Occurrence Records at Any Scale
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Flags common errors in species occurrence records, such as
    coordinates at country centroids, capitals or biodiversity institutions,
    zero or swapped coordinates, records at sea, and duplicates. Each record
    receives one flag per test and nothing is dropped, so any cleaning rule is
    a query over the flags. Proximity tests run as nearest-neighbour queries in
    C++, and records can be streamed from on-disk tables, so a whole GBIF
    snapshot can be flagged on one machine. The tests and their default
    buffers follow 'CoordinateCleaner' (Zizka et al. 2019
    <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13152>).
